  <main_text>
    <l>Pauli Melissi Franci,</l>
    <l>COMITIS SACRI PAL. ET</l>
    <l>EQ̃. CIVIS ROM.</l>
    <l>M E L O S</l>
    <l>AD JACOBVM CHRISTMANNVM</l>
    <l>JOHANNISBERGENSEM.</l>
    <l>ÆTERNITATIS <i>non cluet ultima</i></l>
    <l><i>Pars Tempus, anni syrmata circinans;</i></l>
    <l><i>Volventium astrorum per orbes</i></l>
    <l><i>Fibula firma, tenaxque nexus</i></l>
    <l><i>Labentis ævi. Solem oculum poli,</i></l>
    <l><i>Lunamque vultu degenerem notho,</i></l>
    <l><i>Ad certa subservire par est</i></l>
    <l><i>Momina continuo meatu.</i></l>
    <l><i>Hinc lucis auctor candidus it dies;</i></l>
    <l><i>Hinc umbra noctis furva, nigrantium</i></l>
    <l><i>Mater tenebrarum, diurnos</i></l>
    <l><i>Subsequitur comes atra passus.</i></l>
    <l><i>Aurora porró quotidie recens,</i></l>
    <l><i>Et Vesperugo nascitur indidem:</i></l>
    <l><i>Stellaeque surgunt occiduntque</i></l>
    <l><i>Ordine quaeque suo decenter.</i></l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The abbreviation after "ET" in the third title line is printed as EQ with a tilde over the Q, written here as EQ̃. ("Eq." for eques). Long s is rendered as a plain s throughout, including in "syrmata". Spelling of "Momina" is as printed.</notes>
</page>
